description:
FOUND s501b (Opus, 2026-10-01) by the CPAN board run on Math-BigInt-2.005003 (the #2083 acceptance leg).  PRE-EXISTING in the sense that the code path is old, but NEWLY REACHABLE: on main a0899ba6 every Math::BigRat program died in the #2083 binding-stack recursion (UNIVERSAL::isa delegating to Math::BigFloat's isa override), so this answer was never seen; s501b's #2083 fix turns that crash into this SILENT WRONG answer.

REPRODUCER (scratch/s501b/p/rat3.pl in the s501b worktree; perl 5.40.3 vs PCL at s501b):
    use Math::BigRat;
    for my $s ("3", "49/4", "1/3", "0.5", "-7/2") { my $x = Math::BigRat->new($s); print "$s -> $x\n" }
    my $q = Math::BigRat->new(Math::BigInt->new(49), Math::BigInt->new(4)); print "obj -> $q\n";
  perl: 3 -> 3 / 49/4 -> 49/4 / 1/3 -> 1/3 / 0.5 -> 1/2 / -7/2 -> -7/2 / obj -> 49/4
  PCL : 3 -> 3 / 49/4 -> 1    / 1/3 -> 1   / 0.5 -> 1/2 / -7/2 -> -1   / obj -> 49/4
So only the "N/D" STRING spelling is wrong; the result looks like a truth value (1 / -1 = sign), i.e. something in BigRat::new's string branch (the `m|^\s*([+-]?[^/]+)\s*/\s*(.+?)\s*$|` split, or the `_trim`/`from_*` helpers) returns a boolean where perl returns the captured parts.  Cheap discriminating measurement (not taken): instrument a copy of Math/BigRat.pm's new() (the #2080 method) printing the two captures and the objects built from them.

IMPACT on the board (scratch/s501b/board-tree.log): bigratup.t floor/ceil/bsqrt rows, big_ap.t #3-#5/#15 ('inf'), bitwise-mbr.t (2601 not-ok) are the visible consequences -- these rows were all unreached (0 rows) on the base.
